Ex) Rule 21 (primitive type variable should not be zero)
    {v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≠ 0

[Example Rules]
Rule 15 (broadcasting compatibility for tensor shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) − 1 else ndim(v_2) − 1] : ndim(v_1) − i − 1 < 0 ∨ ndim(v_2) − i − 1 < 0 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − i − 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) − i − 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) − i − 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) − i − 1)

Rule 17 (primitive type variable must be non-negative)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≥ 0

Rule 9 (4D tensor with all shape dimensions positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 4 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 3] : shape(v_1, i) > 0

Rule 28 (list of ints used as dimensions/axes, all non-negative and valid for tensor shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= ∀i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : 0 ≤ v_2[i] ∧ v_2[i] < ndim(v_1)

Rule 11 (index tensor (v_3) is within the input tensor along the specified dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= min(v_3) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_3) ≤ shape(v_1, v_2) − 1

